# Copy to `.env` — it is git-ignored and read by the development launcher.
#
# Client ids for the drive providers that sign in with OAuth. A provider whose
# id is missing reports itself as unavailable rather than offering a connect
# button that could only fail, so you only need the ones you actually use.
#
# Register each as a **desktop/native** client with the redirect URI
#   http://127.0.0.1:47665/drive/callback
# The port is fixed because Dropbox and Microsoft match redirect URIs exactly.
#
# Native apps are public clients and usually get no secret; every flow uses
# PKCE regardless, so the _CLIENT_SECRET lines stay commented out unless the
# provider actually issued one.

POLYMUX_GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_ID=
# POLYMUX_GOOGLE_DRIVE_CLIENT_SECRET=

POLYMUX_DROPBOX_CLIENT_ID=
# POLYMUX_DROPBOX_CLIENT_SECRET=

POLYMUX_ONEDRIVE_CLIENT_ID=
# POLYMUX_ONEDRIVE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Client ids for signing in to a mailbox. By default Polymux reuses the Google
# Drive and OneDrive desktop registrations above; mail still opens its own
# consent flow, so connecting Drive never grants access to email. Add the mail
# variables below only when the provider requires a separate registration.
# Whichever registration is used must also include the redirect URI
# http://127.0.0.1:47666/mail/callback — one port along from the drive flow, so
# connecting a drive and a mailbox at the same moment cannot collide.
#
# Google's IMAP scope (https://mail.google.com/) is restricted, so a client
# using it needs Google's verification before anyone outside the test users can
# sign in. Microsoft's IMAP.AccessAsUser.All and SMTP.Send do not.
# POLYMUX_GOOGLE_MAIL_CLIENT_ID=
# POLYMUX_GOOGLE_MAIL_CLIENT_SECRET=
# POLYMUX_MICROSOFT_MAIL_CLIENT_ID=
# POLYMUX_MICROSOFT_MAIL_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Telegram application identity embedded into desktop builds. Users still sign
# in to their own Telegram account; these remove the per-user API ID/hash step.
POLYMUX_TELEGRAM_API_ID=
POLYMUX_TELEGRAM_API_HASH=
# Optional WeChat writer implementing the JSON stdin/stdout protocol. The
# repository driver supports the helper's verified text, image, file, and video
# paths and fails closed for native-only operations until their ABI is proven.
# POLYMUX_WECHAT_WRITER=/absolute/path/to/Polymux/scripts/polymux-wechat-driver.mjs
# During live development this hard-stops any accidental send outside WeChat's
# File Transfer conversation.
# POLYMUX_WECHAT_TEST_ONLY_FILEHELPER=1
# The released wechatd build omits its LLDB CDN request hook. Point it at the
# copy shipped with Polymux before starting wechatd when developing native
# image, video, voice, or file sending.
# WECHAT_CDN_CAPTURE_SCRIPT=/absolute/path/to/Polymux/scripts/wxcdn_fileid_capture.py
